	charset="us-ascii"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

I was hoping for a method for importing into BioConductor akin to how
marrayInput deals with GenPix and Spot data.  From there I hope to
explore the general functionality of BioConductor for normalization and
ID of differentially expressed genes.
=20
Barry
=20
-----Original Message-----
From: Jess Mar [mailto:jcm@maths.uq.edu.au]=20
Sent: Monday, June 24, 2002 10:45 AM
To: Barry Henderson
Cc: bioconductor@stat.math.ethz.ch
Subject: RE: [BioC] Anyone Working with Imagene Data Files
=20
Sure, what do you want to do with them?
=20
	-----Original Message-----
	From: bioconductor-admin@stat.math.ethz.ch
[mailto:bioconductor-admin@stat.math.ethz.ch]On Behalf Of Barry
Henderson
	Sent: Monday, 24 June 2002 11:54 PM
	To: bioconductor@stat.math.ethz.ch
	Subject: [BioC] Anyone Working with Imagene Data Files
	Hi
	=20
	Is anyone working with Imagene data files?  Imagene creates 2
data files, one for each laser making the data input somewhat more
complicated than for Spot or Genepix. =20
	=20
	Thanks
	=20
	Barry
	=20
